From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:48:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] editor: erosion map boundary (open edges, edge cells follow
 their neighbour, droplet brush reflected, brush window sides) and variation /
 height keeping options

Boundary: the hydraulic solver pinned the outermost ring (fixed height, water sink) while its neighbours were dug, so a wall of untouched ground stood at the map
edge; the erosion brush pinned the whole window, including the sides on the map edge; droplets renormalised / clipped their digging brush at the edge (half the
digging on the border cell); the stream solver did not raise the edge with the uplift and the slide step skipped the ring. Now: edge=open (default) solves the edge
cells with a ghost outflow and lets the outermost cells take the change of their inner neighbour, edge=pinned keeps the old behaviour; brush windows pin only their
sides inside the map; droplet digging reflects at the edge; stream uplift reaches the edge. Tests: border step after every solver and brush mode on tilted fields.

Variation: vary / vary_scale / rain_vary / protect (hard and soft ground, uneven rain, ridges stay), drop_vary, stream jitter, conserve, keep_range, max_change,
brush vary. Droplet speed rule fixed (accel, 0 = old): the old rule slowed droplets down on slopes so they dug almost nothing. New goldens + property tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
